		</ol>

		<div class="cpTabPanels">
					<ol class="tabbedWidgetNarrow cpTabs " role="tablist" aria-hidden="True.ToString().ToLowerInvariant()" style='display: none;'>
						<li class="active" role="presentation">	<a href="#tab161b9142-f5cd-4bf9-af49-d789cbe256bd_0" class="tabButton" id="tabBtnNarrow161b9142-f5cd-4bf9-af49-d789cbe256bd_0" role="tab" aria-controls="tab161b9142-f5cd-4bf9-af49-d789cbe256bd_0" aria-selected="true" tabindex="0"><span class="tabName editable" data-sequence="0" data-tabname="English" contenteditable="false">English</span></a>
</li>
					</ol>
				<div class="tabbedWidget cpTabPanel showing" style="" id="tab161b9142-f5cd-4bf9-af49-d789cbe256bd_0" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tabBtn161b9142-f5cd-4bf9-af49-d789cbe256bd_0" tabindex="-1">

<div class="widget editor pageStyles narrow" id="divEditor823e84c8-7921-4898-8760-cba7b1a5c013" data-elementqueryclasses='{"wide-narrow":"min-width:25em"}'>
	    <div class="fr-view">


        <p>On September 16th, 2024, the Hayward Area Recreation and Park District (H.A.R.D.) transitioned from at-large to by-district elections. This was due to recent legal challenges under the Federal Voting Rights Act, which prompted many municipalities, counties, and districts to shift to by-district or division elections. On May 20, 2024, the H.A.R.D. The Board of Directors adopted a resolution expressing the District&rsquo;s intention to move to district-based elections.</p><p><span dir="ltr" id="isPasted">This transition towards more equitable representation highlights H.A.R.D.&apos;s dedication to serving its diverse community effectively and</span> aligns with the District&apos;s commitment to Justice, Equity, Diversity, and Inclusion (JEDI).</p>
    </div>

<script type="text/javascript">
	$(document).ready(function (e) {		
	    renderSlideshowIfApplicable($('#divEditor' + '823e84c8-7921-4898-8760-cba7b1a5c013'));
	});
</script>
</div>

				</div>
					<ol class="tabbedWidgetNarrow cpTabs " role="tablist" aria-hidden="True.ToString().ToLowerInvariant()" style='display: none;'>
						<li class="" role="presentation">	<a href="#tab161b9142-f5cd-4bf9-af49-d789cbe256bd_1" class="tabButton" id="tabBtnNarrow161b9142-f5cd-4bf9-af49-d789cbe256bd_1" role="tab" aria-controls="tab161b9142-f5cd-4bf9-af49-d789cbe256bd_1" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1"><span class="tabName editable" data-sequence="1" data-tabname="Espa&#241;ol" contenteditable="false">Español</span></a>
</li>
					</ol>
				<div class="tabbedWidget cpTabPanel " style="display: none;" id="tab161b9142-f5cd-4bf9-af49-d789cbe256bd_1" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tabBtn161b9142-f5cd-4bf9-af49-d789cbe256bd_1" tabindex="-1">

<div class="widget editor pageStyles narrow" id="divEditorf28d67cc-db1f-4b17-b76c-478a70924630" data-elementqueryclasses='{"wide-narrow":"min-width:25em"}'>
	    <div class="fr-view">


        <p data-placeholder="Translation" aria-label="Translated text" data-ved="2ahUKEwizo-Cg3_6GAxWtJzQIHc00KJgQ3ewLegQIBxAT" dir="ltr" id="isPasted">El Distrito de Parques y Recreaci&oacute;n del &Aacute;rea de Hayward (H.A.R.D.) actualmente lleva a cabo elecciones generales. Sin embargo, recientes impugnaciones legales en virtud de la Ley Federal de Derecho al Voto han llevado a muchos municipios, condados y distritos a pasar a elecciones por distritos o divisionales. Recientemente, H.A.R.D. recibi&oacute; una notificaci&oacute;n de una posible violaci&oacute;n de la Ley de Derecho al Voto de California, alegando que las elecciones generales dilu&iacute;an el poder de voto de los votantes asi&aacute;tico-americanos. En respuesta, H.A.R.D. est&aacute; comprometido con la transici&oacute;n a elecciones por distrito, aline&aacute;ndose con su compromiso con la Justicia, la Equidad, la Diversidad y la Inclusi&oacute;n (JEDI).<br><br>Adem&aacute;s, AB 350 proporciona un proceso de &ldquo;puerto seguro&rdquo; para la redistribuci&oacute;n de distritos, lo que permite a los municipios evitar litigios contra la CVRA mediante la adopci&oacute;n de resoluciones y la participaci&oacute;n en foros comunitarios para facilitar la transici&oacute;n a elecciones por distrito.<br><br>El 20 de mayo de 2024, el H.A.R.D. La Junta Directiva adopt&oacute; una resoluci&oacute;n expresando la intenci&oacute;n del Distrito de pasar a elecciones basadas en el distrito. DURO. organizar&aacute; cuatro reuniones comunitarias en los centros comunitarios locales (Cherryland Community Center, San Felipe Community Center, Sorensdale Community Center y San Lorenzo Homes Associations) para garantizar una s&oacute;lida participaci&oacute;n y aportaciones de los residentes. Adem&aacute;s, el Distrito llevar&aacute; a cabo cinco reuniones p&uacute;blicas en la Oficina del Distrito para revisar el proceso de distritaci&oacute;n, examinar mapas y, en &uacute;ltima instancia, adoptar los l&iacute;mites finales del distrito.<br><br>Este paso proactivo hacia una representaci&oacute;n equitativa resalta la dedicaci&oacute;n de H.A.R.D. para servir a su comunidad diversa de manera efectiva.</p><p data-placeholder="Translation" aria-label="Translated text" data-ved="2ahUKEwizo-Cg3_6GAxWtJzQIHc00KJgQ3ewLegQIBxAT" dir="ltr">Para obtener m&aacute;s informaci&oacute;n sobre el proceso y ver c&oacute;mo utilizar DistrictR para trazar sus propios l&iacute;mites electorales de distrito, siga este <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3Y-2gQD-AhM" target="_blank" rel="noopener">enlace&nbsp;</a>o haga clic en la imagen a continuaci&oacute;n:</p><p data-placeholder="Translation" aria-label="Translated text" data-ved="2ahUKEwizo-Cg3_6GAxWtJzQIHc00KJgQ3ewLegQIBxAT" dir="ltr"><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3Y-2gQD-AhM"><img src="/ImageRepository/Document?documentId=10167" class="fr-dib" alt="Districting 101 HARD 7.1.24" style="width: 351px;"></a></p>
    </div>

<script type="text/javascript">
	$(document).ready(function (e) {		
	    renderSlideshowIfApplicable($('#divEditor' + 'f28d67cc-db1f-4b17-b76c-478a70924630'));
	});
</script>
</div>

				</div>
					<ol class="tabbedWidgetNarrow cpTabs " role="tablist" aria-hidden="True.ToString().ToLowerInvariant()" style='display: none;'>
						<li class="" role="presentation">	<a href="#tab161b9142-f5cd-4bf9-af49-d789cbe256bd_2" class="tabButton" id="tabBtnNarrow161b9142-f5cd-4bf9-af49-d789cbe256bd_2" role="tab" aria-controls="tab161b9142-f5cd-4bf9-af49-d789cbe256bd_2" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1"><span class="tabName editable" data-sequence="2" data-tabname="简体中文" contenteditable="false">简体中文</span></a>
</li>
					</ol>
				<div class="tabbedWidget cpTabPanel " style="display: none;" id="tab161b9142-f5cd-4bf9-af49-d789cbe256bd_2" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tabBtn161b9142-f5cd-4bf9-af49-d789cbe256bd_2" tabindex="-1">

<div class="widget editor pageStyles narrow" id="divEditor60e6be83-7501-4da1-8815-db898d4d1716" data-elementqueryclasses='{"wide-narrow":"min-width:25em"}'>
	    <div class="fr-view">


        <p>海沃德地区休闲公园区 (H.A.R.D.) 目前正在进行普选。然而，最近《联邦投票权法》下的法律挑战促使许多市、县和区转向按区或分区选举。最近，H.A.R.D.收到可能违反《加州投票权法》的通知，指控普选削弱了亚裔美国选民的投票权。作为回应，H.A.R.D.致力于过渡到分区选举，以符合其对正义、公平、多样性和包容性 (JEDI) 的承诺。<br id="isPasted"><br>此外，AB 350 还提供了重新划分选区的&ldquo;安全港&rdquo;流程，允许市政当局通过决议和参与社区论坛来避免 CVRA 诉讼，以促进向分区选举的过渡。<br><br>2024 年 5 月 20 日，H.A.R.D.董事会通过了一项决议，表达了该区转向以区为基础的选举的意图。难的。将在当地社区中心（Cherryland 社区中心、San Felipe 社区中心、Sorensdale 社区中心和 San Lorenzo Homes Associations）举办四次社区会议，以确保居民的积极参与和投入。此外，学区将在学区办公室举行五次公开会议，审查选区流程、检查地图并最终采用最终的学区边界。<br><br>这一迈向公平代表性的积极举措凸显了 H.A.R.D. 致力于有效服务其多元化社区</p><p>要了解有关该过程的更多信息并了解如何使用 DistrictR 绘制您自己的选区选举边界，请点击此链接或单击下图：</p><p><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3Y-2gQD-AhM" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="/ImageRepository/Document?documentId=10167" class="fr-dib" alt="Districting 101 HARD 7.1.24" style="width: 357px;"></a></p>
    </div>

<script type="text/javascript">
	$(document).ready(function (e) {		
	    renderSlideshowIfApplicable($('#divEditor' + '60e6be83-7501-4da1-8815-db898d4d1716'));
	});
</script>
</div>

				</div>
					<ol class="tabbedWidgetNarrow cpTabs " role="tablist" aria-hidden="True.ToString().ToLowerInvariant()" style='display: none;'>
						<li class="" role="presentation">	<a href="#tab161b9142-f5cd-4bf9-af49-d789cbe256bd_3" class="tabButton" id="tabBtnNarrow161b9142-f5cd-4bf9-af49-d789cbe256bd_3" role="tab" aria-controls="tab161b9142-f5cd-4bf9-af49-d789cbe256bd_3" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1"><span class="tabName editable" data-sequence="3" data-tabname="Tagalog" contenteditable="false">Tagalog</span></a>
</li>
					</ol>
				<div class="tabbedWidget cpTabPanel " style="display: none;" id="tab161b9142-f5cd-4bf9-af49-d789cbe256bd_3" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tabBtn161b9142-f5cd-4bf9-af49-d789cbe256bd_3" tabindex="-1">

<div class="widget editor pageStyles narrow" id="divEditor742d93ae-d10a-4112-9a80-e31b6fc84d84" data-elementqueryclasses='{"wide-narrow":"min-width:25em"}'>
	    <div class="fr-view">


        <p>Ang Hayward Area Recreation and Park District (H.A.R.D.) ay kasalukuyang nagsasagawa ng at-large na halalan. Gayunpaman, ang mga kamakailang legal na hamon sa ilalim ng Federal Voting Rights Act ay nag-udyok sa maraming munisipalidad, county, at distrito na lumipat sa by-district o division elections. Kamakailan, ang H.A.R.D. nakatanggap ng paunawa ng isang posibleng paglabag sa California Voting Rights Act, na nagsasaad na ang mga malawakang halalan ay nagpapahina sa kapangyarihan sa pagboto ng mga botanteng Asian American. Bilang tugon, sinabi ni H.A.R.D. ay nakatuon sa paglipat sa mga halalan sa by-district, na umaayon sa pangako nito sa Justice, Equity, Diversity, and Inclusion (JEDI).<br id="isPasted"><br>Bukod pa rito, ang AB 350 ay nagbibigay ng proseso ng &quot;safe harbor&quot; para sa muling pagdistrito, na nagpapahintulot sa mga munisipalidad na maiwasan ang paglilitis sa CVRA sa pamamagitan ng pagpapatibay ng mga resolusyon at pagsali sa mga forum ng komunidad upang mapadali ang paglipat sa mga halalan sa by-district.<br><br>Noong Mayo 20, 2024, ang H.A.R.D. Pinagtibay ng Lupon ng mga Direktor ang isang resolusyon na nagpapahayag ng intensyon ng Distrito na lumipat sa mga halalan na nakabatay sa distrito. MAHIRAP. magho-host ng apat na pagpupulong ng komunidad sa mga lokal na sentro ng komunidad (Cherryland Community Center, San Felipe Community Center, Sorensdale Community Center, at San Lorenzo Homes Associations) upang matiyak ang matatag na pakikipag-ugnayan at input ng mga residente. Dagdag pa rito, ang Distrito ay magsasagawa ng limang pampublikong pagpupulong sa Opisina ng Distrito upang suriin ang proseso ng pagdistrito, suriin ang mga mapa, at sa huli ay magpatibay ng mga huling hangganan ng distrito.<br><br>Ang aktibong hakbang na ito tungo sa pantay na representasyon ay nagtatampok sa dedikasyon ng H.A.R.D. sa epektibong paglilingkod sa magkakaibang komunidad nito.</p><p>Upang matuto nang higit pa tungkol sa proseso at makita kung paano gamitin ang DistrictR upang gumuhit ng iyong sariling Mga Hangganan sa Halalan sa Distrito, mangyaring sundan ang <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3Y-2gQD-AhM" target="_blank" rel="noopener">link&nbsp;</a>na ito o mag-click sa larawan sa ibaba:</p><p><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3Y-2gQD-AhM" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="/ImageRepository/Document?documentId=10167" class="fr-dib" alt="Districting 101 HARD 7.1.24" style="width: 323px;"></a></p>
    </div>

<script type="text/javascript">
	$(document).ready(function (e) {		
	    renderSlideshowIfApplicable($('#divEditor' + '742d93ae-d10a-4112-9a80-e31b6fc84d84'));
	});
</script>
</div>

